{:edb/db-before-t 1533 :edb/db-after-t 1534 :edb/tx-data [[13194139534846 50 #inst "2026-10-08T08:54:18.049Z" 13194139534846 true] [17592186063993 1100 "Evaluate $\\displaystyle \\int_0^{1/2}x(1-2x)^5\\,\\textrm d x$." 13194139534846 false] [17592186063993 1100 "Evaluate $\\displaystyle \\int_0^{1/2}x(1-2x)^5\\,\\textrm d x.$" 13194139534846 true] [17592186063993 1145 "Let $u=1-2x$. Then, we have\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{\\textrm d u}{\\textrm d x} = -2\\quad\\Longrightarrow\\quad -\\dfrac 1 2 \\,\\textrm d u = \\textrm d x\n$$\n\nWe also note that\n\n$$\nx = \\dfrac 1 2 (1-u)\n$$\n\nComputing our limits of integration, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}x & 0 & 1/2 \\\\ u & 1 & 0\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nWe can now solve the integral using our new variable $u$, remembering to use the new limits of integration:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n∫_{0}^{1/2}x(1 - 2x)^{5}dx &= ∫_{1}^{0}\\frac{1}{2} \\cdot (1 - u) \\cdot u^{5} \\cdot (-\\frac{1}{2})du \\\\\n&=-\\frac{1}{4}∫_{1}^{0}(1 - u) \\cdot u^{5}du \\\\\n&=-\\frac{1}{4}∫_{1}^{0}(u^{5} - u^{6})du \\\\\n&=-\\frac{1}{4}(\\frac{1}{6}u^{6} - \\frac{1}{7}u^{7}) \\mid _{1}^{0} \\\\\n&=-\\frac{1}{4}([0 - 0] - [\\frac{1}{6} - \\frac{1}{7}]) \\\\\n&=-\\frac{1}{4}(-\\frac{1}{42}) \\\\\n&= \\frac{1}{168}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534846 false] [17592186063993 1145 "Let $u=1-2x.$ Then, we have\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{\\textrm d u}{\\textrm d x} = -2\\quad\\Longrightarrow\\quad -\\dfrac 1 2 \\,\\textrm d u = \\textrm d x.\n$$\n\nWe also note that $x = \\dfrac 1 2 (1-u).$ \n\nComputing our limits of integration, we get\n\n| **$x$** | $0$ | $1/2$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| **$u$** | $1$ | $0$ |\n\nWe can now solve the integral using our new variable $u,$ remembering to use the new limits of integration:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{1/2}x(1-2x)^{5}\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{1}^{0}\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot (1-u)\\cdot {u}^{5}\\cdot (-\\frac{1}{2})\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{4}{\\int }_{1}^{0}(1-u)\\cdot {u}^{5}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{4}{\\int }_{1}^{0}({u}^{5}-{u}^{6})\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{4}{(\\frac{1}{6}{u}^{6}-\\frac{1}{7}{u}^{7})|}_{1}^{0} \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{4}([0-0]-[\\frac{1}{6}-\\frac{1}{7}]) \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{4}(-\\frac{1}{42}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{168}\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534846 true] [17592186063994 1100 "Calculate $\\displaystyle \\int x^3\\sqrt{x^2 + 1}\\, \\textrm{d}x$." 13194139534846 false] [17592186063994 1100 "Calculate $\\displaystyle \\int x^3\\sqrt{x^2 + 1}\\, \\textrm{d}x.$" 13194139534846 true] [17592186063994 1145 "Let\n\n$$\nu = x^2+1\n$$\n\nThen, we have\n\n$$\n\\frac{du}{dx} = 2x⟹\\frac{1}{2}du = xdx\n$$\n\nWe can now solve the integral in terms of $u$, and then express our final answer in terms of $x$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n∫x^{3}\\sqrt{x^{2} + 1}dx &= ∫x^{2} \\cdot x\\sqrt{x^{2} + 1}dx \\\\\n&= ∫x^{2}\\sqrt{x^{2} + 1} \\cdot xdx \\\\\n&= ∫x^{2}^(⏞)^(u - 1)\\sqrt{x^{2} + 1} \\cdot xdx^(⏞)^(\\frac{1}{2}du) \\\\\n&= ∫(u - 1)\\sqrt{u} \\cdot \\frac{1}{2}du \\\\\n&= \\frac{1}{2}∫(u - 1)u^{1/2}du \\\\\n&= \\frac{1}{2}∫(u^{3/2} - u^{1/2})du \\\\\n&= \\frac{1}{2}(\\frac{2}{5}u^{5/2} - \\frac{2}{3}u^{3/2}) + C \\\\\n&= \\frac{1}{5}(x^{2} + 1)^{5/2} - \\frac{1}{3}(x^{2} + 1)^{3/2} + C \\\\\n&= \\frac{1}{5}\\sqrt{(x^{2} + 1)^{5}} - \\frac{1}{3}\\sqrt{(x^{2} + 1)^{3}} + C\n\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534846 false] [17592186063994 1145 "Let $u = x^2+1.$ Then, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=2x\\,⟹\\,\\frac{1}{2}\\text{d}u=x\\,\\text{d}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can now solve the integral in terms of $u,$ and then express our final answer in terms of $x\\mathbin{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int {x}^{3}\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+1}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int {x}^{2}\\cdot x\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+1}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int {x}^{2}\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+1}\\,\\cdot x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int \\overset{u-1}{\\overset{⏞}{{x}^{2}}}\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+1}\\cdot \\overset{\\frac{1}{2}\\text{d}u}{\\overset{⏞}{x\\,\\text{d}x}} \\\\  & =\\int (u-1)\\sqrt{u}\\cdot \\frac{1}{2}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\int (u-1){u}^{1/2}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\int ({u}^{3/2}-{u}^{1/2})\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}(\\frac{2}{5}{u}^{5/2}-\\frac{2}{3}{u}^{3/2})+C \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{5}({x}^{2}+1)^{5/2}-\\frac{1}{3}({x}^{2}+1)^{3/2}+C \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{5}\\sqrt{({x}^{2}+1)^{5}}-\\frac{1}{3}\\sqrt{({x}^{2}+1)^{3}}+C\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534846 true] [17592186064121 1020 #edb/ref 17592186314343 13194139534846 true] [17592186064121 1020 #edb/ref 17592186314357 13194139534846 true] [17592186064121 1020 #edb/ref 17592186314360 13194139534846 true] [17592186064121 1020 #edb/ref 17592186314377 13194139534846 true] [17592186064122 1020 #edb/ref 17592186314329 13194139534846 true] [17592186064122 1020 #edb/ref 17592186314336 13194139534846 true] [17592186064122 1020 #edb/ref 17592186314350 13194139534846 true] [17592186064122 1020 #edb/ref 17592186314363 13194139534846 true] [17592186064122 1020 #edb/ref 17592186314370 13194139534846 true] [17592186064412 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139534846 true] [17592186064412 1100 "Evaluate the integral ${\\int }_{-2}^{0}x{(x+2)}^{3}\\,\\text{d}x.$" 13194139534846 true] [17592186064412 1100 "Evaluate the integral $∫_{-2}^{0}x(x + 2)^{3}dx$." 13194139534846 false] [17592186064412 1145 "Let $u=x+2.$ Then, we have\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=1\\,⟹\\,\\text{d}x=\\text{d}u.\n$$\n\nWe also note that $x=u-2.$\n\nComputing our limits of integration, we get\n\n| **$x$** | $-2$ | $0$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| **$u$** | $0$ | $2$ |\n\nWe can now solve the integral using our new variable $u,$ remembering to use the new limits of integration:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{-2}^{0}x{(x+2)}^{3}\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}(u-2){u}^{3}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}({u}^{4}-2{u}^{3})\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & ={(\\frac{1}{5}{u}^{5}-2\\cdot \\frac{1}{4}{u}^{4})|}_{0}^{2} \\\\  & ={(\\frac{1}{5}{u}^{5}-\\frac{1}{2}{u}^{4})|}_{0}^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{5}({2}^{5}-{0}^{5})-\\frac{1}{2}({2}^{4}-{0}^{4}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{5}(32-0)-\\frac{1}{2}(16-0) \\\\  & =\\frac{32}{5}-8 \\\\  & =-\\frac{8}{5}\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534846 true] [17592186314329 1017 #edb/ref 17592186314330 13194139534846 true] [17592186314329 1089 "q-113751" 13194139534846 true] [17592186314329 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139534846 true] [17592186314329 1100 "Given that $u=x+1,$ which integral is equivalent to $\\int \\frac{{x}^{2}}{\\sqrt{x+1}}\\,\\text{d}x?$" 13194139534846 true] [17592186314329 1113 #uuid "e75208f3-66d2-5336-8c11-cf16a17b2543" 13194139534846 true] [17592186314329 1145 "Since $u=x+1,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=1\\,⟹\\,\\text{d}u=\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nWe also note that \n$x=u-1.$\n\nNow we can rewrite the integral in terms of $u:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{{x}^{2}}{\\sqrt{x+1}}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int \\frac{(u-1)^{2}}{\\sqrt{u}}\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\int ({u}^{2}-2u+1){u}^{-1/2}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\int ({u}^{3/2}-2{u}^{1/2}+{u}^{-1/2})\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\int (\\sqrt{{u}^{3}}-2\\sqrt{u}+\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{u}})\\,\\text{d}u\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534846 true] [17592186314330 1000 #edb/ref 17592186314331 13194139534846 true] [17592186314330 1000 #edb/ref 17592186314332 13194139534846 true] [17592186314330 1000 #edb/ref 17592186314333 13194139534846 true] [17592186314330 1000 #edb/ref 17592186314334 13194139534846 true] [17592186314330 1000 #edb/ref 17592186314335 13194139534846 true] [17592186314330 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139534846 true] [17592186314330 1041 "selection" 13194139534846 true] [17592186314330 1104 #edb/ref 17592186314335 13194139534846 true] [17592186314330 1110 #uuid "c05f6cf4-27df-5e4f-9f0c-9635ab289308" 13194139534846 true] [17592186314331 1034 "\\int (\\sqrt{{u}^{3}}-2\\sqrt{{u}^{2}}+\\frac{1}{u})\\,\\text{d}u" 13194139534846 true] [17592186314331 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534846 true] [17592186314331 1111 #uuid "c6a9cf29-9efc-5527-a29a-1330ac2270d1" 13194139534846 true] [17592186314332 1034 "\